   "about": "A detailed survey of Japanese fishery production, fishing grounds, processing industries and domestic distribution.",
   "summary": "The report continues with shellfish and oyster culture, then examines deep-sea fishing in home, northern, Soviet and colonial waters. It surveys seaweed, whaling, fur seals, sea otters and pearl culture before describing drying, freezing, canning, fish meal, fish oil and agar-agar production. Its final pages begin a discussion of domestic fish markets, rail transport and prices. Tables give prewar production, fleet, processing and market figures; the report continues beyond page 319.",
